sweet-mali-smbind (lowclk 2026-11-15, research 164 part B1 levers 2 and 3): boot-arg sweetsmbind=<mask> for the Mali completion thread sm_thread (bsd/dev/sweet_mali.c). CODE ONLY: no register access, no new hardware write, no new firmware command, no new bus store (the existing JOB interrupt routing, GICD_IROUTER = boot CPU at pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c:336, is not touched), so there is nothing new for AGENTS rule 8 to review; the only scheduler calls are the ones this file already uses (thread_bind + thread_block in mem_probe_cpu, kernel_thread_start).
sweetsmbind absent or 0: behavior byte-identical to patch 0364 (kernel_thread_start as before, never bound; only never-taken branches added).
Bit 0 (1): bind sm_thread to the cpu that takes SPI 452 = master_cpu = ml_get_boot_cpu_number() (every sweet SPI is routed to affinity 0.0.0.0 = the boot CPU, pe_fiq.c:336 + :234 [obs SWEET CPU: cpu=0 mpidr=0x0]; arm_init.c:435; not hardcoded). Prints `SWEET MALI: sm_thread bound to cpu N (sweetsmbind=V)`; a missing processor or a failed bind is a SWEET MALI GAP line and the thread stays unbound.
Bit 1 (2): create sm_thread at priority 93 = BASEPRI_PREEMPT_HIGH instead of 81 (kernel_thread_start passes -1 = BASEPRI_KERNEL, thread.c:1960; bands in osfmk/kern/sched.h: BASEPRI_KERNEL 81, BASEPRI_PREEMPT 92, BASEPRI_PREEMPT_HIGH 93, MAXPRI_KERNEL 95, BASEPRI_REALTIME 96). Priorities of the other threads that must keep running: USB log drain thread ud_log_thread 81 (kernel_thread_start), sweet_wdt pet = thread_call KERNEL_HIGH group 92 (thread_call.c), the stall detector is a timer_call (interrupt context, not a thread), thread_call HIGH group 93, thread_call daemon 94. sm_thread runs about 3.5 % of one core [obs K17 CPUTOP] and blocks between jobs, so it is not expected to starve them [guess, not measured]. Prints `SWEET MALI: sm_thread priority 81 -> 93 (sweetsmbind=V ...)` (old value is read from source, not measured).
Other bits: GAP line, ignored.
Log only, needs sweetcomplat=1 (the ISR stamp of patch 0364): once per second `SWEET PERF: complat_wake wake_same N wake_other M isr_cpu C bound_cpu B sweetsmbind V`: per consumed JOB-interrupt stamp, the cpu sm_isr ran on (written before the stamp with a release fence) against cpu_number() in sm_thread after lck_mtx_sleep_deadline returned. Printed on its own row, so the 0364 complat row is unchanged.
Host test: tools/test_sweet_smbind365.py compiles the pure block between SMBIND-PURE-BEGIN/END and checks every hook with mutants. Not run on hardware. The new write path (none) is unreviewed; the thread-priority and bind change is a scheduling change a reviewer may still want to look at.
